            </profile>
            <profile id="991d-bfd7-a5e0-849b" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="af20-e256-4a51-93aa" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapons, throwing spear, light armour and shield. May have javelins (+1 pt). May be mounted on a horse (+8 pts). Warband. Werod. 0-1 unit. If included in the army the Righ must accompany this unit at all times (not enforced). Dal Riata: the unit may be Stubborn (+3 pts per model). Scotland: may exchange throwing spear for thrusting spear (free) and pay +1 pt per model to use Shieldwall. Picts: count as light infantry and may be equipped with pike (+1 pt). Strathclyde: count as light infantry if not mounted, light cavalry if mounted. (Shieldwall p.30)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="1f96-647c-3b88-7356" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">5+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
