  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="2f3c-b74f-47dc-5ae0" name="Caledonians (Shieldwall) - List Notes" publicationId="af20-e256-4a51-93aa" hidden="false">
      <description>CALEDONIAN ARMY LISTS (Shieldwall, pp.26-32): Dal Riata, Alba, the Picts, Scotland and Strathclyde. Percentages are by points. Special rules pp.4-5 and 29 (Raiders: the Caledonian commander may always choose whether he moves first or second).
The Common/Uncommon pools differ between the compositions, so the units also belong to pool categories named after them (Common Warriors: ... / Uncommon Warriors: ...).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Dal Riata]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: Toisech, Soer-chele and Doer-chele: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: Eachraidh and Dogs of War: up to 25%
  Dal Riata (p.28). Characters up to 33%; Toisech, Soer-chele and Doer-chele at least 50%; Eachraidh and Dogs of War (Vikings, Amsaigh, Gasraidh) up to 25%. The unit of Toisech may be Stubborn (+3 pts). All Soer-chele cost 6 pts, have Leadership 6 and use throwing spears, not thrusting spears; any unit of Soer-chele may be designated as light infantry for free.
[Alba]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: Toisech, Soer-chele and Doer-chele: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: Eachraidh and Dogs of War: up to 25%
  Alba (p.28). Characters up to 33%; Toisech, Soer-chele and Doer-chele at least 50%; Eachraidh and Dogs of War (Vikings, Amsaigh, Gall-Gaedhil, Gasraidh) up to 25%. Every other unit of Doer-chele may have bows (+1 pt).
[The Picts (the Cruithne)]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: Toisech, Soer-chele and Doer-chele: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: Eachraidh and Dogs of War: up to 25%
  The Picts (p.28). Characters up to 33%; the army may not include the Righ. Toisech, Soer-chele and Doer-chele at least 50%; Eachraidh and Dogs of War (Vikings, Gasraidh) up to 25%. All Toisech and Soer-chele count as light infantry and may be equipped with pike (+1 pt). Every other unit of Doer-chele may have bows (+1 pt) or hunting crossbows (free).
[Scotland]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: Toisech and Soer-chele: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: Doer-chele, Eachraidh and Dogs of War: up to 33%
  Scotland (p.28). Characters up to 33%; Toisech and Soer-chele at least 50%; Doer-chele, Eachraidh and Dogs of War (Vikings, Gall-Gaedhil, Freebooters, Stipendarii) up to 33%. The Toisech may exchange throwing spear for thrusting spear (free) and may pay an additional +1 pt per model to use Shieldwall. The Soer-chele cost 6 pts, are equipped with shields and may use Shieldwall. Every other unit of Doer-chele may have bows (+1 pt).
[Strathclyde]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: Toisech, Eachraidh, Soer-chele and Doer-chele: at least 50%
  Dogs of War: up to 25%
  Strathclyde (p.28). Characters up to 33%; the army may not include the Righ; one Mormaer may become Army General for +25 pts. Toisech, Eachraidh, Soer-chele and Doer-chele at least 50%; Dogs of War (Vikings only) up to 25%. Toisech count as light infantry if not mounted, light cavalry if mounted. Units of Eachraidh may exchange javelins for throwing spears (free). All units of Soer-chele count as light infantry.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
